import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';
---

<LegalLayout title="Privacy Policy" heading="Privacy Policy" description="Privacy Policy for Public IPTV: what contact, subscription and technical data we collect, why, retention periods and your rights.">
  <p>
    Public IPTV (“we”, “our”) provides IPTV subscriptions that start with a free
    trial. This policy explains what personal data we collect, why we collect it,
    and the rights you have. If anything here is unclear, contact us at
    contact@public-iptv.online.
  </p>
  <h2 style="font-size: 24px; margin-top: 8px;">1. Data we collect</h2>
  <p>
    <strong>Contact details:</strong> your email address and anything you include
    in messages to us (such as your device type or the number of screens you
    watch on), used to create trial logins, deliver setup details and answer
    support requests.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Subscription records:</strong> plan type, start date and billing
    status, used to operate your account and apply the refund policy.
  </p>
  <p>
    <strong>Technical data:</strong> basic server logs (such as IP address and
    user agent) collected automatically for security and abuse prevention. We do
    not run advertising trackers, and this website ships no third-party
    analytics scripts.
  </p>
  <h2 style="font-size: 24px; margin-top: 8px;">2. How we use it</h2>
  <p>
    We use your data only to provide the service: activating trials, managing
    subscriptions, responding to support, preventing fraud, and meeting legal
    obligations. We never sell personal data and never share it with advertisers.
  </p>
  <h2 style="font-size: 24px; margin-top: 8px;">3. Sharing and processors</h2>
  <p>
    Data is shared only where necessary to run the service — for example email
    delivery and payment processing — under contracts that limit use to our
    instructions. If a processor changes, this policy is updated.
  </p>
  <h2 style="font-size: 24px; margin-top: 8px;">4. Retention</h2>
  <p>
    Trial contact data is kept while your account is active and for up to 12
    months afterwards for support continuity, then deleted. Billing records are
    kept as long as tax and accounting law requires. Server logs rotate within
    90 days.
  </p>
  <h2 style="font-size: 24px; margin-top: 8px;">5. Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    You may request access, correction, export or deletion of your personal data
    at any time by emailing contact@public-iptv.online. We respond to every
    request personally. If you believe your rights were violated, you can also
    complain to your local data-protection authority.
  </p>
  <h2 style="font-size: 24px; margin-top: 8px;">6. Security</h2>
  <p>
    Accounts are protected by unique credentials sent to your email. Keep them
    confidential and tell us immediately if you suspect misuse. No method of
    internet transmission is perfectly secure, but we limit internal access to
    the minimum needed to operate support and billing.
  </p>
  <h2 style="font-size: 24px; margin-top: 8px;">7. Changes</h2>
  <p>
    Material changes to this policy are announced on this page with a new “last
    updated” date before they take effect.
  </p>
  <p>Last updated: 2026-10-04.</p>
</LegalLayout>
